% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `bitmap`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class body
% is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3).  Window M8's rest
% (2026-11-26): the one method the held paragraph image code sends to it.
% USAGE: `:get_plane_count(#bitmap, N)` (window.md §2.13; paragraph
% p_imag.esp:601, :616 color_check/1 and color_check2/1, the PSI/UX edits
% of 1991 that replaced `:get_parameter(#ipl, bmm_size, Dev)`; p_v_imag.esp
% :111-117; gog-esp DISPB1.ESP:36): 1 plane is monochrome (p_imag.esp:596
% -604: N > 1 is colour), and so are 07FF's (window.md §2.13).

class bitmap has

% :get_plane_count(#bitmap, N) -- INTERPOLATED (body OURS): the stand-in's
% screen is the 1-bit frame of psi/winfb.py (OURS, the hardware plan
% §2.1), so 1.
:get_plane_count(_, 1);

end.
